 "brief": "A spring clip in PETG (FDM, printed flat so the layers stack along Z) that holds a 25 mm broom handle on a wall. The wall is the plane y = 0. One M4 screw goes through the back of the clip into the wall at x = 0, z = 0. The handle runs along Z with its centre at y = 18 and snaps in through a 20 mm mouth facing away from the wall. The clip is 16 mm tall (z = -8 to 8) and stays inside x = -19 to 19, y = 0 to 33. A handle yanked sideways out of the clip pushes each jaw tip outward with up to 40 N. Safety factor 2.",
